# Working output of the parity tooling: `band.py` writes cropped comparisons and
# `shoot_port.sh` writes the port frames the diffs read. Both are regenerated in one
# command, so committing them only creates a second copy that goes stale silently.
# (`tools/reference/pwa/` and `port2/` ARE committed — they are the baseline the diff
# compares against and CI has no browser to re-shoot them.)
tools/reference/band/

# Godot writes a .uid next to every script; they are how the editor tracks a
# script across a rename and are meant to be committed. Kept, deliberately.
